data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Mechanism:** Cas9 nuclease paired with a synthetic guide RNA cuts the genome at a chosen site [1]. This adapts a bacterial system that stores phage DNA fragments to destroy similar viruses in later infections [2].\n\n- **Edit types:** Targeted insertion, deletion, or substitution defines gene editing. CRISPR is one of several tools alongside zinc finger nucleases and TALENs [3].\n\n- **Reported applications (unverified):** Headlines describe CRISPR as a possible treatment for a broad range of diseases [4] and report HIV elimination in cell culture [5]. Only the headlines were reviewed, so these claims need full-study confirmation."}

